    <string name="map_centred_on_me">Centred on you</string>
    <!--
      The overview control and the bar down the edge of the map. The bar's
      caption says "straight line" because that is what it measures: the app
      has no routing engine, and a bar that implied it knew the road would be
      wrong by however much the road bends.
    -->
    <string name="map_overview">See the whole route</string>
    <string name="map_progress_straight_line">direct</string>
    <!--
      The same bar, when the server managed to fetch a road route: the number
      above it is then road distance measured along that route, not the gap to
      the finish. The two are wildly different on a mountain road, so which one
      is on screen is said rather than left to be guessed.
    -->
    <string name="map_progress_by_road">by road</string>
    <!--
      Shown when the trail is on and there is nothing to draw. Without it, a
      switched-on trail with no history is indistinguishable from a switched-on
      trail that is broken — which is exactly how it read on a real ride.
    -->
    <string name="map_no_position">No position yet</string>
    <string name="map_last_seen">Last known position</string>
    <string name="map_you">%1$s (you)</string>
    <string name="map_no_location">Couldn\'t work out where you are. Check that location is on.</string>
    <string name="map_speed_kmh">%1$d km/h</string>
    <!-- No speed to show: an older build, or a fix whose provider had none. -->
    <string name="map_speed_unknown">—</string>
    <string name="map_own_speed">Your speed</string>
    <!--
      When this phone last had a report accepted. Shown only while sharing.
      The service has always recorded it and nothing showed it, which made a
      ride where positions stopped landing look exactly like one where they
      landed and the screen failed to draw them.
    -->
    <string name="map_reported_now">Sent just now</string>
    <string name="map_reported_minutes">Sent %1$d min ago</string>
    <!--
      How old a rider's last reported position is. Shown because positions
      arrive on a cadence rather than continuously: a pin that has not moved
      is usually correct, and without this it is indistinguishable from a
      dead app.
    -->
    <string name="map_fix_age_now">just now</string>
    <string name="map_fix_age_minutes">%1$d min ago</string>
    <!--
      The list order is worked out from which way the group is heading, not
      from distance along a road — the app has no route to measure against.
      The row says so, because a bare "in front first" would read as a fact.
    -->
